==Restrictions==
Unit Restriction: Only [[Kabuto Cat (Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]], [[Kuwagata Cat (Special Cat)|Kuwagata Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N202 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N202]]

==Battleground==
*1 [[Ursamajor]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*5 [[White Wind]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 9.33 seconds<sup>280f</sup>.
*5 [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 8.67 seconds<sup>260f</sup>.
*7 [[White Wind]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 7.33 seconds<sup>220f</sup>.
*7 [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is advised to get [[Kuwagata Cat (Special Cat)|King Kuwagata Cat]] to Lv.45 before even attempting this stage, and you can forget about timed rewards without a Lv.55 King Kuwagata and [[Kabuto Cat (Special Cat)|Golden Kabuto Cat]] at your disposal. In truth, Ursamajor hardly poses anything remotely close to a threat prior to Strengthening; however, that quickly flips on its head as soon as he does. It is very easy to lose ground due to bad luck in [[Ancient Egg: N202 (Special Cat)|Armored Firefly Cat]] Weaken procs or Li'l Doge Dodges. Just keep spamming your bugs at a constant rate to act as a blockade until you can get a few good hits in on the boss. It's not over once he reaches the base either, since you can use the frontliners to build up momentum behind your Cat Base and hone in for a counterpush. Strong/Attack UP [[Cat Combo]]s are heavily recommended.

